llama : MoE cache - pin the host experts, and report where a step goes

Pinning (phase 2 of docs/moe-offload-plan.md in EuLLM). The experts the cache
copies from are registered with the GPU backend when the cache is created, so
that a miss is uploaded by DMA at the bus's full speed instead of being staged
through a driver buffer from pageable memory; the large-batch copies the
copy callback makes from the same tensors gain the same way. Only the expert
pages are pinned, in page-aligned ranges merged where tensors share a page,
and only if they leave a quarter of the RAM and at least 8 GiB to everything
else. LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_PIN=0 leaves them pageable. Experts loaded without mmap
are in the backend's pinned host buffer already and are left alone. One line
on stderr says what was pinned, or why not; a failure suggests loading
without mmap, since some drivers refuse to pin a read-only file mapping
("operation not supported" on the reference PC). The cache spans several
GPUs since llama.cpp #30112; the pages are pinned once, through the backend of
the first GPU that caches experts, which registers them as portable for all.

Statistics (phase 1). LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_STATS=N prints to stderr, every N steps
of up to 8 tokens that went through the cache, the time per step split into
the time until each layer's router was read back, the time in the cache
(planning and issuing the uploads) and the rest; the MiB uploaded and the
share of experts found in VRAM; and, from one step in 8 that waits for its
uploads, how long uploading takes and at what rate. The cache's totals at
exit go to stderr as well while the statistics are on.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp b11925. Needs 0001 to pin.

